er, so the control plane stays available even when individual nodes go down.","originalFile":"Kubernetes provides a declarative configuration model for managing containerized applications. The platform serves as a robust foundation for orchestrating workloads across clusters, leveraging its built-in scheduling capabilities to ensure high availability.\n\nAdditionally, the ecosystem has garnered significant attention from enterprise adopters. Industry reports highlight the crucial role that container orchestration plays in the evolving landscape of cloud-native development, underscoring the importance of standardized deployment patterns.\n\nThe control plane features a distributed key-value store (etcd) that maintains cluster state. It boasts automatic failover and leader election, ensuring that the system remains operational during node failures.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":5,"lines":["-Kubernetes provides a declarative configuration model for managing containerized applications. The platform serves as a robust foundation for orchestrating workloads across clusters, leveraging its built-in scheduling capabilities to ensure high availability.","+Kubernetes uses a declarative configuration model for managing containerized applications. You describe the desired state, and the scheduler places workloads across nodes to keep things running if something fails."," ","-Additionally, the ecosystem has garnered significant attention from enterprise adopters. Industry reports highlight the crucial role that container orchestration plays in the evolving landscape of cloud-native development, underscoring the importance of standardized deployment patterns.","+Enterprise adoption has grown steadily since 2020. The CNCF's 2023 survey found that 84% of organizations either use or evaluate Kubernetes, mostly to standardize how they deploy and run services across environments."," ","-The control plane features a distributed key-value store